11.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round-4 split unchanged (B bloc 14 vs C bloc 8). B continues to dominate on geometry: poly(dT) capture + 75×225 is strictly 3′-anchored; CDR3 (400–600 nt upstream) remains outside Read 2 reach on every molecule. TSO insertion after UMI converts to 5′-RACE/template-switching, places CDR3 inside the 225 bp read, preserves bead barcoding/UMI/Abseq/Sample-Tag/mRNA panels/Rhapsody workflow/fixed sequencing config, and matches BD’s commercial immune-repertoire module exactly. Minor open variable: routine TSO-density titration on mixed beads.

C bloc reiterates that flanking TCR oligos (V/leader + constant) physically anchor the full junction at hybridization so the 225 bp read traverses CDR3 without repositioning the start site or altering the validated schematic. They assert this is a minimal surface-only titration already supported by BD mixed-oligo protocols. No rebuttal has emerged to the positional fact that capture remains 3′-anchored unless the flanking oligos fully supplant poly(dT) for TCR transcripts (which is never stated). Commercial BD module precedent and the explicit “same bead schematic” constraint both favor B; C’s physical-anchoring claim does not overcome the distance problem inside the fixed read length.

Persistent conclusion: B remains the single minimal, architecture-correct solution satisfying every stated constraint. No new empirical data or decisive factual correction appeared.}

